There are other creatures than nymphs that give teleportitis, without a
chance of giving teleport control. They share more abilities with
nymphs.

What I do when I happen to have a tinning kit is to tin several tengu,
until I have about five or so of them. Only then will I eat those tins.
If I accidentally get teleportitis from them, I still have a fair chance
of getting control as well.

> I also avoid molds, except for the slime mold, because I recall
> that eating at least one of them can kill me.

Some of them are poisonous, indeed, but not all. Others may stun you or
make you hallucinate (try hallucination once with a starting character:
it's hilarious the first time it happens to you!).

>> That *was* spoily, I guess, especially since you had already sort of
>> figured out that your pet could also be used in this way.

>    Figured out, no, I actually *read* that :(. That would be
